import frappe

# No blank lines: sync finds the block by the next blank line.
AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS = """\
Gameplan (gameplan app):
Gameplan is an async discussions app. The UI says Community for GP Team and Space for GP Project.
- Call document methods with call_document_method.
- A Space belongs to a Community through its team field. A GP Discussion belongs to a Space through its project field.
- GP Task and GP Page are deprecated. Do not create them or suggest them to people.
- Replies are GP Comment with reference_doctype "GP Discussion" and reference_name set to the discussion name. Closed discussions take no new replies.
- content fields are HTML. Mention a person with <span class="mention" data-type="mention" data-id="<user email>" data-label="<full name>">@<full name></span>.
- Find a person's email with call_method gameplan.api.search_users {"query": "<name or email>"}.
  Add "direct_messages": true to list only people who accept direct messages.
- Create discussions and replies with call_method gameplan.approvals.submit: pass doctype ("GP Discussion" or "GP Comment"), a unique request_key, and HTML content; discussions also need project and title, replies need discussion. A GP Submission result is held privately for approval. Do not bypass it with create_document. Do not update project, closed_at or pinned_at. Use these GP Discussion methods instead: move_to_project {"project": "<space>"}, close_discussion, reopen_discussion, pin_discussion {"pin_scope": "Space" or "Category"} (Category pins it in the Community), unpin_discussion.
- Track your submissions with call_method gameplan.approvals.queue; omit community and choose status Pending, Approved, Rejected, or Withdrawn. Do not create GP Submission or GP Approval Counter directly.
- Posting limits apply to new discussions and replies, including pending submissions. Check your wait with call_method gameplan.posting_limits.status {"kind": "discussion" or "reply"}. Respect retry_after seconds and preserve drafts. Global admins configure limits in Admin settings > Posting rules. Never write GP Posting Event directly. Per-post limits cap links, images, files/videos and mentions per forum post. A refused post names the limit it exceeded; remove the extra items and submit again.
- Check your reply cooldown with call_method gameplan.slow_mode.status {"discussion": "<name>"}; respect retry_after seconds. Moderators change it with gameplan.slow_mode.set_mode {"discussion": "<name>", "seconds": 30, "expected_seconds": 0, "reason": "<why>"}. Use seconds 0 to disable; expected_seconds is the current policy. Optionally end it automatically with duration_seconds 3600/86400/604800/2592000 or a timezone-bearing ends_at; status returns ends_at. Do not write slow_mode_seconds, slow_mode_until or GP Slow Mode State directly.
- Mark a discussion as read with call_method gameplan.api.set_discussion_read_state {"discussion": "<name>"}; pass "unread": true to mark it unread. This also works for banned readers and archived Spaces. Mark a whole Space with GP Project mark_all_as_read.
- Community admins appoint existing members with gameplan.api.set_community_moderator {"community": "<name>", "user": "<email>", "is_moderator": 1 or 0}. Appointment never grants private-Space access.
- Trust levels are site-wide: 0 New, 1 Basic, 2 Contributor, 3 Regular, 4 Leader. They are off until a global admin turns them on with call_method gameplan.trust_levels.save_settings {"enabled": 1}; get_settings lists every requirement, which save_settings also accepts. Global admins set a level with gameplan.trust_levels.set_level {"user": "<email>", "level": 2, "reason": "<why>"} and hold it with set_lock {"user": "<email>", "locked": 1, "reason": "<why>"}. They list people at one level with gameplan.api.search_users {"trust_level": "2"}, or "pending" for people not worked out yet, and sort by level with {"order_by": "trust_level"}. While levels are on, a Community admin holds posts from members below a level for approval with gameplan.approval_policy.set_level_policy {"community": "<name>", "min_level": "Basic", "Contributor" or ""}. A member reads their own level and next requirements with call_method gameplan.trust_levels.my_level (POST).
- Moderators use GP Discussion or GP Comment hide or delete_spam {"reason": "<reason, at most 500 characters>"}, get_hidden_content to preview, and restore {"reason": "<optional>"}. Public attachments must become private before removal.
- Badges are earned automatically and are off until a global admin turns them on with call_method gameplan.badges.api.save_settings {"enabled": 1}. Read them with gameplan.badges.api.list_badges and user_badges {"user": "<email>"}. Admins also read who holds a badge with badge_holders {"badge": "<key>"}, and list_badges gives them each badge's holder count. Choose your own favourites with set_favorites {"badges": ["<key>"]} (at most 3). Global admins grant_badge or revoke_badge {"user": "<email>", "badge": "<key>", "reason": "<reason>"}. Do not create GP User Badge directly.
- Weighted auto-hide: while trust levels are on, a Community admin turns it on with call_method gameplan.auto_hide.save_settings {"community": "<name>", "enabled": 1, "threshold": 6} (3 to 30); moderators read it with gameplan.auto_hide.get_settings. Spam and Abuse/inappropriate reports add the reporter's weight (New and Basic 1, Contributor 2, Regular, Leader and Community staff 3). At the threshold the post is hidden until review and its review shows auto_hidden. In gameplan.reporting.resolve, Dismiss restores such a post and Hide, Uphold or Delete Spam keep it removed. Restoring it any other way dismisses its reports too.
- Global admins manage whole-site restrictions with call_method gameplan.restrictions.set_restriction {"user":"<email>","enabled":1,"reason":"<reason>","duration_seconds":3600,"kind":"Silence" or "Suspend"}; set enabled 0 with a reason to lift. Silence blocks participation in every Community but keeps sign-in and reading; Suspend blocks sign-in and API access across the site. A person has one site restriction at a time. Remove all of a person's posts as spam with call_method gameplan.author_cleanup.start {"user":"<email>","reason":"<reason>","community":"<Community>"}; omit community (global admins only) to clean up every Community. It runs in the background and appears in Community moderation History, where gameplan.author_cleanup.undo {"cleanup":"<cleanup id>"} restores the posts it removed. Optional community scopes this action to a Community ban. Use duration_seconds 0/3600/86400/604800/2592000 or timezone-bearing expires_at for a custom deadline, not both. Re-read current state before changing it and send expected_modified. Global lists/history: gameplan.restriction_queries.account_suspensions and account_history. Restrictions preserve content and pending submissions.
- List removed content with call_method gameplan.moderation.removed_content {"community": "<name>", "doctype": "GP Discussion" or "GP Comment", "start": 0}.
- Moderators ban participation with call_method gameplan.community_bans.set_ban {"community": "<name>", "user": "<email>", "banned": 1, "reason": "<reason>"}; use banned 0 with a reason to lift it. Optional expires_at is an ISO datetime with timezone. List active bans with gameplan.moderation.community_bans {"community": "<name>", "start": 0} (40 rows per page plus one lookahead row). Bans preserve reading and survive rejoining.
- React to a GP Discussion, GP Comment or GP Poll with its react method, args {"operations": [{"emoji": "👍", "operation": "add" or "remove"}]}. Bookmark with add_bookmark and remove_bookmark.
- Direct messages are private to the people in them, and only work for people who turned them on: gameplan.direct_messages.set_direct_messages_enabled {"enabled": 1}. Send with call_method gameplan.direct_messages.send_message {"to": "<email>", "content": "<html>"}, or {"conversation": "<id>", "content": "<html>"} to reply; add "reply_to": <message id> to quote a message. Read with gameplan.direct_messages.get_conversations and get_messages {"conversation": "<id>"} (add "around": <message id> to open at a message; its "seen" says up to which message, and when, the others have read); mark read with mark_read {"conversation": "<id>"}, or every chat with mark_all_read. Find chats and messages with search {"query": "<text>"}. List the files or links shared in a chat with get_shared_messages {"conversation": "<id>", "kind": "files"} ("links" for links; add "query": "<text>" to narrow, "before": <message id> for older). Change or remove your own message with edit_message {"message": <id>, "content": "<html>"} and delete_message {"message": <id>}. React with react {"message": <id>, "emoji": "👍"}; the same call again takes it back. Mute with set_muted {"conversation": "<id>", "muted": 1}; to stop notifications for every chat while keeping unread counts, call gameplan.gameplan.doctype.gp_user_profile.gp_user_profile.save_my_notification_preferences {"preferences": {"direct_message_notifications": 0}}. Delete a chat from your own list with clear_conversation {"conversation": "<id>"}; the other person keeps it. Block someone with block_user {"user": "<email>"} so neither of you can message the other (group chats are not affected); undo with unblock_user {"user": "<email>"}, and list who you blocked with get_blocked_users. Do not read or write GP Conversation, GP Conversation Member, GP Message or GP User Block directly.
- Vote with GP Poll submit_vote {"option": "<option title>"}. Undo with retract_vote.
- Search posts with call_method gameplan.api.search_sqlite, args {"query": "<text>"}.
- Change membership with GP Project join, leave, add_member {"user": "<email>"} and remove_member, or GP Team add_members {"users": ["<email>"]} and remove_member.
- People allowed by Admin settings > Who can invite people (Gameplan admins always) invite with call_method gameplan.api.invite_by_email, args {"emails": "<comma separated emails>", "role": "Gameplan Member"}.
- A site can turn off direct messages, polls, tags or search, and can set the shortest and longest discussion title, the shortest post, whether titles may repeat, who may create tags, who may use @everyone and who may start a direct conversation. A refused post or action names the rule; change the content to fit, do not retry it unchanged. Global admins read these with call_method gameplan.site_settings.get_settings and change several at once with save_settings {"values": {"<setting>": <value>}}, which saves all of them or none. Never write GP Settings directly.
- Do not create or edit GP Reaction, GP Bookmark, GP Unread Record, GP Discussion Visit or GP Notification. They hold each person's own state.
- Watched words: Community/global admins manage Block, Censor, Require approval and Flag rules through gameplan.watched_words.rules/add/remove. Use gameplan.watched_words.upload with a private File ID to preview CSV; pass its returned expected token to apply it. Never write GP Watched Word directly. Use gameplan.watched_word_edits.original to load an authorized original, then gameplan.watched_word_edits.submit with doctype, name, expected_modified, content, and discussion title to save or queue an edit. A GP Submission result means the published version remains unchanged until approval.
""".strip()  # noqa: E501
AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS_HEADING = AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.splitlines()[0]


def sync_agent_instructions():
	"""Write the current guide into System Settings > Agent Instructions on install and migrate.

	Gameplan's block runs from its heading to the next blank line. It is replaced in place, or appended
	when missing. Text outside the block is kept.
	"""
	# Frappe versions without the built-in MCP server have no such field.
	if not frappe.get_meta("System Settings").has_field("agent_instructions"):
		return

	current = frappe.db.get_single_value("System Settings", "agent_instructions") or ""
	before, heading, after = current.partition(AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS_HEADING)
	if heading:
		_block, blank_line, rest = after.partition("\n\n")
		instructions = before + AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS + blank_line + rest
	elif current.strip():
		instructions = f"{current.rstrip()}\n\n{AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS}"
	else:
		instructions = AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS

	if instructions != current:
		frappe.db.set_single_value("System Settings", "agent_instructions", instructions)
